  13: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
  14:     """Slide every colored object rightward until it is blocked by the edge or by an object that started farther right.
  15: 
  16:     Input structure
  17:     A black-background grid contains several monochromatic foreground objects, each a 4-connected component.
  18: 
  19:     Rule
  20:     Clear the foreground, then process objects from right to left by their original bounding boxes.
  21:     Each object keeps its shape and color while repeatedly moving one cell to the right until its next step would leave the grid or overlap an already placed object.
  22: 
  23:     Key insight
  24:     The objects behave like horizontal gravity: rightmost objects settle first and become blockers, so later objects cannot pass through them even if there is empty space beyond.
  25:     """
  26:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
  27:     assert g.ndim == 2
  28: 
  29:     bg = get_bg(g)
  30:     components = find_components(g, bg=bg, connectivity=4, monochromatic=True)
  31:     assert components
